{
  "note": "Which Element Plus component each manifest is compared against, and what the two call the same thing. The identifiers are Element Plus's own: a tag from the editor metadata it publishes (el-button) or a component directory, for the components that metadata does not cover (message-box). `rename` maps an Element Plus prop to the name this library gives it. `equiv` names an Element Plus prop this library expresses as a value of another prop. `skipGroups` names the Element Plus props this library deliberately does not carry, grouped by why: a prop that needs JavaScript, a value the host supplies, data for the host to render, a component to put in a slot, a place in the DOM, a duration, an attribute of the native element, or a style string the host passes. Everything Element Plus declares that is not in a skip group and not in this library is a gap — and a gap is a failure.",
  "source": {
    "package": "element-plus",
    "version": "2.14.9"
  },
  "skipGroups": {
